{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And HaShem strengthened Pharaoh's heart.</b> It is not in the nature of a man to endure these plagues and still be able to stand without his heart dying within him. And now Scripture has made clear the wickedness of Pharaoh and the cruelty of his heart, for he persisted in his rebellion through the first five plagues — there the strengthening of the heart came from himself, through his own wickedness and folly. But from the fifth plague onward — the plague of pestilence (דבר), concerning which it is written, ״ויכבד לב פרעה ולא שלח את העם״ — the strengthening of his heart was caused by the Almighty, and this is what is said: ״ויחזק ה׳ את לב פרעה״, to teach that the nations are in the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, like clay in the hand of the potter. And so Yirmeyahu said (Jeremiah 18:6): ״הנה כחומר ביד היוצר כן אתם בידי בית ישראל״, and it is written immediately after it: ״רגע אדבר על גוי ועל ממלכה״ and so forth. And similarly Shelomo said (Mishlei 21): ״פלגי מים לב מלך ביד ה׳ על כל אשר יחפוץ יטנו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:39.101160643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}